  ('634cc9a0-2742-567c-8aa1-5e705afd5bbc'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'PERSONAL_INTRODUCTION', E'PERSONAL_INTRODUCTION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '634cc9a0-2742-567c-8aa1-5e705afd5bbc'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - PERSONAL_INTRODUCTION - 1', E'Please introduce yourself to the examiner. You may talk about where you come from, what you study or do for work, your interests, and your plans for the future.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('643994e8-6a17-56fe-8140-93b4c589093a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '643994e8-6a17-56fe-8140-93b4c589093a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - READ_ALOUD - 1', E'Hopefully, this will treat and prevent acne and other skin diseases and reduce antibiotic use. Naked Biome is entering clinical trials to see if its approach is safe and effective.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('39e5f219-4f39-5e72-8402-dbc706384aca'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '39e5f219-4f39-5e72-8402-dbc706384aca'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - READ_ALOUD - 2', E'Researchers have found a way to convert the aromatic substance vanillin into a redox-active electrolyte material for liquid batteries. The technology is an important step towards ecologically sustainable energy storage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('693153d8-81d4-50d5-bb39-00c66eb329df'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'READ_ALOUD', E'READ_ALOUD', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '693153d8-81d4-50d5-bb39-00c66eb329df'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - READ_ALOUD - 3', E'Straddling Asia and Europe across the strait, the old city of Istanbul, Turkey, has embraced diverse cultural influences. Known for its monumental architecture, Istanbul has become a cherished travel destination.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f7f92f03-ffa8-54d1-a4d4-a9a5fab4b450'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'f7f92f03-ffa8-54d1-a4d4-a9a5fab4b450'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - REPEAT_SENTENCE - 1', NULL, '61d65127-fdc2-54f2-919b-f73d58b879fa'::uuid, NULL, E'Next time, we''ll discuss the influence of the media on public policy.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('320c6927-1c59-5774-8639-87fe3987d027'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '320c6927-1c59-5774-8639-87fe3987d027'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - REPEAT_SENTENCE - 2', NULL, '80fe2c51-b577-57ca-a30e-3042ced65a2e'::uuid, NULL, E'He would yell if he was interrupted while painting.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('28c7f468-c5f4-5568-9374-52ced2c50525'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'REPEAT_SENTENCE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '28c7f468-c5f4-5568-9374-52ced2c50525'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - REPEAT_SENTENCE - 3', NULL, '5afe61c6-21b8-588f-9d9a-db7ae0cf17e4'::uuid, NULL, E'Please come to the next seminar properly prepared.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a5e1430a-056a-51ee-99ef-1c6236ba25d8'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'DESCRIBE_IMAGE', E'DESCRIBE_IMAGE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'a5e1430a-056a-51ee-99ef-1c6236ba25d8'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - DESCRIBE_IMAGE - 1', NULL, NULL, '43240762-3b6a-51e1-9621-fc5b7750110c'::uuid, E'The bar chart shows the average monthly rainfall in Newtown from January to June. Rainfall is highest in January at 78 millimetres and falls steadily every month, reaching its lowest point of 25 millimetres in June.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('c28a1784-8245-5d9d-9aae-30ed1a96edf1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'DESCRIBE_IMAGE', E'DESCRIBE_IMAGE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'c28a1784-8245-5d9d-9aae-30ed1a96edf1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - DESCRIBE_IMAGE - 2', NULL, NULL, 'b3392ff5-e8a8-566f-ad51-94f2150461e1'::uuid, E'The line graph shows how many people shopped online in a small country between 2019 and 2023. The number rose every year, from 120 thousand to 440 thousand, with the sharpest increase between 2020 and 2021.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('5fe93d85-c902-596a-a459-66f2df78e13c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'DESCRIBE_IMAGE', E'DESCRIBE_IMAGE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '5fe93d85-c902-596a-a459-66f2df78e13c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - DESCRIBE_IMAGE - 3', NULL, NULL, '4e374d5e-350d-5195-91c8-d2dcf2bc9325'::uuid, E'The pie chart shows how a household spends its monthly income. Housing takes the largest share at 35 percent, followed by food at 25 percent, while leisure accounts for the smallest share at only 10 percent.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('a8cb6218-7521-5b4f-97d8-57ac726e0d5b'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'a8cb6218-7521-5b4f-97d8-57ac726e0d5b'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - RE_TELL_LECTURE - 1', NULL, '847bdd21-07fb-5bc8-8f8d-daa7a0c0b330'::uuid, NULL, E'So there are two theories for how the gas giants formed. One is the same theory I showed you just now core accretion, right. And the other is called disk instability and one of our colleagues at DTM has done a lot of work on that and so it''s unclear exactly how they formed but you''re right what we''re trying to do the reason we''re trying to get the higher and higher pressure in the lab is because we are trying to understand more about the pressure inside the gas giants. It''s thought that the gas giants also have a metallic core, but maybe the metallic core not made of iron. Hydrogen, for example becomes metallic at a certain pressure. So it''s very possible that the insides of these planets could have metallic cores, could have hydrogen cores, could have rocky portions we''re not sure. But the higher pressure we can get in the lab, the closer we can get understanding the interiors of the gas giants and the exoplanet that are so big.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('50e82bce-9f8b-5149-9566-1dabe6e42692'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '50e82bce-9f8b-5149-9566-1dabe6e42692'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - RE_TELL_LECTURE - 2', NULL, '048654eb-63ee-5a47-b00d-c49322ef6b05'::uuid, NULL, E'Hello everyone. Today''s lecture is about setting up a website. I''m going to be focusing on things that you need to consider to ensure your website really adds value to the people using it.\nSo - there are three main areas you need to think about. The first and most important thing is who is your target audience? When you''re creating a new website you really need to think about who the users are and what\ninformation they''ll be looking for. What we do when we set up websites is to group users based on their needs. So, for a website in the academic community, for example, we may have groups such as researchers and administrators, and this helps us design the site and add information that is relevant to each group.\nThe second point is accessibility. The main thing here is to ensure your website can be found. And you can do this by making sure it can be reached from areas on the web where your target audience are also active. So this may mean providing links on other websites or maybe using social media.\nAnd thirdly - retention-making sure your target audience return to your website regularly. You do this by ensuring it gives them a reason to come back. So it''s important to keep the site up-to-date and make sure it provides the latest news and interesting information and so on.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('1adba967-b00d-5643-9011-a16db38ec79c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'RE_TELL_LECTURE', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '1adba967-b00d-5643-9011-a16db38ec79c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - RE_TELL_LECTURE - 3', NULL, 'e440314d-b74b-5f48-b358-4ca10c3fc47c'::uuid, NULL, E'Super-symmetry is a mathematical idea that people have developed an effort to understand the sharpest organising principle for the fundamental constituents of matter. You see, we have learned that particles that seem to be different, can actually secretly be united by certain symmetry principles. So we use the fact that there are symmetric objects in the world like a sphere or basketball. You turn a sphere, and even though you''ve transformed it, it looks the same fundamentally. We found that certain particles when you transform one particle into another, even though looks like the identity of the particle has changed, overall the equations describing it they don''t change at all at an underlying level of symmetry, but we''ve not been able to do is find a symmetry that would relate certain kinds of particles, namely matter particles and force particles. Matter particles are particles like electrons, muons and quarks, force particles are like photons and gluons and WZ bosons. Super-symmetry is a symmetry that actually relates to these two kinds, these two classes of particles. And people have proven that super-symmetry is the last possible symmetry of the fundamental particles that are mathematics, reality has not yet been shown to make use of it. So people are now trying to see whether that symmetry might actually be working in the world can be found evidence for it in our understanding of fundamental particles.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('52211a70-b4ca-5722-ac92-56796b165299'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '52211a70-b4ca-5722-ac92-56796b165299'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION - 1', E'Who discovered gravity?', 'e632a44e-0fb6-5dfc-b648-0f1f588d49a7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Newton', NULL, NULL),
  ('73a40f1d-bc99-55cd-9512-e07befce10cd'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '73a40f1d-bc99-55cd-9512-e07befce10cd'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION - 2', E'Who cuts men''s hair?', '28896c7a-7c9b-5034-b899-1e29d7fc18db'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Barber / hairdresser', NULL, NULL),
  ('b93971da-6b02-59da-beb1-d959c746f0fe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'b93971da-6b02-59da-beb1-d959c746f0fe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION - 3', E'How do butterflies fly?', '02f50a1d-51e4-553b-9fdc-cf2599e01ba7'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Flutter', NULL, NULL),
  ('285f16bf-c69b-5d00-b54b-081305b7cbd9'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION', E'SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '285f16bf-c69b-5d00-b54b-081305b7cbd9'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION - 1', NULL, '685838c2-b57e-5122-a2fe-431516d317a6'::uuid, NULL, E'I think working from home is the best change in modern work. People save hours of travel every day and have more time for their families. I agree it saves time, but I see a problem. Many employees feel isolated at home, and it is harder for new staff to learn from colleagues. That is true, yet companies can solve this. A hybrid model, with two or three office days a week, keeps teams connected and still reduces commuting. Hybrid sounds fair, but not every manager trusts staff who are out of sight. Some still measure hours instead of results. Exactly. If managers focus on results, remote work succeeds. If they focus on presence, it fails. There is also the cost. Offices are expensive, and a smaller office could save a company a great deal of money. Those savings could pay for better home equipment and for regular team meetings in person. So we all accept that flexibility matters, but we disagree about how much time people should spend in the office.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f8a6e7b0-69f4-5df4-a7bc-95b0ddfab9fe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION', E'SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'f8a6e7b0-69f4-5df4-a7bc-95b0ddfab9fe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION - 2', NULL, '823be9b1-dd3a-595b-bc0a-62d754903946'::uuid, NULL, E'Our city should spend more money on public transport. Buses and trains reduce traffic and cut air pollution. I support better transport, but the money has to come from somewhere. Higher taxes would upset many residents. Perhaps the fares could rise slightly for people who can afford it, while students and older people keep cheap tickets. Cheap tickets matter. If a ticket costs too much, people go back to using their cars. Cars will not disappear soon, though. Many people live far from any station and need a way to get home. Then we need local feeder buses and safe bicycle lanes, not just new train lines. A good network also attracts businesses, so the investment returns money to the city over time. I agree with that, as long as the plan is clear about costs and the work is finished on schedule.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b8931334-bae3-5057-b2d7-5b480fcca435'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION', E'SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'b8931334-bae3-5057-b2d7-5b480fcca435'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION - 3', NULL, 'a8a802ab-f6e8-5a7a-972a-3ae612d77218'::uuid, NULL, E'School uniforms make every student look equal. Nobody feels judged for the clothes their family can or cannot afford. That is a fair point, but uniforms also limit personal expression. Teenagers want to show who they are. I think uniforms save time in the morning, and parents do not have to buy many fashionable clothes. They also create a sense of belonging, like a team wearing the same colours. However, uniforms are not free. Some schools require expensive items that must be bought from one shop. Then schools could allow simple clothes in a few agreed colours, which would be cheaper and more flexible. That compromise keeps equality without forcing every family to spend a lot. I would accept that, provided students can still choose how they dress on special days.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('0078b35b-a0c3-522b-b4a7-a9c098f5b2ab'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '0078b35b-a0c3-522b-b4a7-a9c098f5b2ab'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION - 1', E'You have submitted a wrong file to your manager. Please apologize to him for it.', 'd8a3e6ae-32c2-5374-90a6-3a5659e391e4'::uuid, NULL, E'Respected manager, I hope you are doing well.\nI would like to discuss an issue we have encountered with my submitted file.\nIt appears that I mistakenly sent you the incorrect file, and I sincerely apologize for this careless mistake.\nI would appreciate your opinion on this matter. Thank you for your consideration.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('d874fc45-cc5d-5e8f-98d7-ffac2cc64060'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'd874fc45-cc5d-5e8f-98d7-ffac2cc64060'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION - 2', E'Your flatmate doesn''t follow the schedule to complete housework. What would you say to him or her?', 'bcb4f5f1-507c-5d5a-945b-765f77708fce'::uuid, NULL, E'Hey flatmate, I want to talk to you about something.\nWe seem to have a little issue with our housework schedule.\nIt''s like you haven''t finished your housework following our agreed schedule.\nAnd I''d like to know what you think.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('f5aea024-a339-550f-bdb3-3470dd3ada96'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION', E'SPEAKING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'f5aea024-a339-550f-bdb3-3470dd3ada96'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION - 3', E'You are ten minutes late for a meeting because of a traffic jam. How should you explain to your colleagues?', '71fcf48b-90b0-5182-9d2a-92e98a5f67d2'::uuid, NULL, E'Hey everyone, I want to talk to you about something.\nWe seem to have a little issue with my arrival for the meeting.\nIt''s like I was stuck in a traffic jam, which made me ten minutes late for this meeting.\nAnd I''d like to know what you think.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('b10f1aab-614e-57e7-8f1a-6422d38eb5ad'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'b10f1aab-614e-57e7-8f1a-6422d38eb5ad'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT - 1', E'As we have already seen, the American economy is increasingly global and effects of a downturn in one area of the world can immediately affect the value of American stocks at home. Throughout the first half of the year, it was widely speculated that Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan would choose to raise interest rates in the US to cool down the economy a bit and prevent inflation from creeping in. By late September, though, he was coming under increasing pressure to lower interest rates to fend off deflationary pressure. What happened?', NULL, NULL, E'the American economy is increasingly global, with a downturn in one area of the world able to immediately affect the value of American stocks at home, and although it was widely speculated that Greenspan would choose to raise interest rates in the US to cool down the economy and prevent inflation, he was coming under increasing pressure to lower interest rates to fend off deflationary pressure.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('e235ec83-746b-556f-9a1b-e2033480243f'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'e235ec83-746b-556f-9a1b-e2033480243f'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT - 2', E'In order to have a competitive edge, athletes often use drugs with high athletic performance.\nThe National Honey Board recently found that honey has the same functions but less negative impact. This clinical trial is the third in a series of studies focusing on the use of honey by athletes. The first study (involving 71 subjects) determined that honey has a milder effect on blood sugar than other popular forms of carbohydrate gel.\nThe second study in the series (with 39 weight trained subjects) investigated the combination of honey with a protein supplement and suggested that honey speeds muscle recovery after a workout.', NULL, NULL, E'Honey, with the same functions as drugs used by athletes for high athletic performance and less negative impact, has a milder effect on blood sugar than other popular forms of carbohydrate gel, and speeds muscle recovery after a workout.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('675e406f-2fb4-5db1-a275-d35471481090'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT', E'WRITING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '675e406f-2fb4-5db1-a275-d35471481090'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT - 3', E'Negotiation is a common process in business to mainly solve business conflicts between both parties. Compromise is a basic negotiation state in which both parties give up something that they want in order to get something else they want more. Compromise usually occurs in unfair parties when there is a fixed pie to be divided up, and whatever on one side gets, the other side loses.\nIn compromise situations, neither side gets all of what they really want, but they each make concessions in order to reach an agreement that is acceptable to both. Both parties usually can reach a win-win situation through compromise. However, negotiation cannot resolve all the conflict if one party is unwilling to resolve the problem.', NULL, NULL, E'Negotiation is a common process in business to mainly solve business conflicts between both parties, and compromise is a basic negotiation state in which both parties give up something, which usually occurs in unfair parties when there is a fixed pie to be divided up, so they each make concessions to reach an agreement that is acceptable to both, but negotiation cannot resolve the conflict if one party is unwilling to resolve the problem.', NULL, 5, 75),
  ('c835ed1e-b0ba-5776-811e-c9fb438f6012'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'c835ed1e-b0ba-5776-811e-c9fb438f6012'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - WRITE_ESSAY - 1', E'Working employees have paid leave. Is it good or bad?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('97f02440-9145-56ee-b548-21e6e9e8fd93'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '97f02440-9145-56ee-b548-21e6e9e8fd93'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - WRITE_ESSAY - 2', E'Globalization is important. What is your opinion? Give your reasons.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('f38811b6-e27e-5b37-8a6e-8b184b19d009'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITE_ESSAY', E'WRITING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'f38811b6-e27e-5b37-8a6e-8b184b19d009'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - WRITE_ESSAY - 3', E'What potential challenges do students face in online learning environments?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 200, 300),
  ('8bb31149-9648-55b8-a45a-b26572f01305'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '8bb31149-9648-55b8-a45a-b26572f01305'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN - 1', E'Research has suggested that major stressors in our lives are life {{1}} , for example, moving house, marriage or relationship breakdown. Work-related factors, {{2}} unemployment and boredom, are also common {{3}} of stress. Differences in personality may also {{4}} a part.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.changes, 2.including, 3.causes, 4.play', NULL, NULL),
  ('bf54fab9-694b-5d8b-b657-1a69565a8a1d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'bf54fab9-694b-5d8b-b657-1a69565a8a1d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN - 2', E'Farmers {{1}} fertilize their fields to ensure healthy crop growth. Fertilizer {{2}} a strong effect on agricultural productivity. The real {{3}} is that farmers often do not know {{4}} fertilizer they should use, which can lead either to poor yields or to harmful overuse.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.should, 2.has, 3.problem, 4.how much', NULL, NULL),
  ('ff0baae9-ba03-535c-ab7d-95f105e2254c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'ff0baae9-ba03-535c-ab7d-95f105e2254c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN - 3', E'Climate is the word we {{1}} for weather over a long period of time. The desert has a dry climate because there is very little rain. The UK {{2}} a ‘temperate climate’, {{3}} means winters are, overall, mild and {{4}} , generally, don’t get too hot.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.use, 2.has, 3.which, 4.summers', NULL, NULL),
  ('f0fe488f-3b14-5510-86fe-d0dfbe88419d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'f0fe488f-3b14-5510-86fe-d0dfbe88419d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_READING_MULTIPLE - 1', E'By the laws of probability, most decisions made under pressure should be flawed ones, yet psychologists have found that people routinely make correct judgments most of the time, even with limited information. One of Gladwell''s surprising points is that we can actually learn how to make better snap judgments, in the same way that we can learn logical, deliberative thinking. But first we have to accept the idea that thinking long and hard about something does not always deliver us better results, and that the brain actually evolved to make us think on our feet.\n\nWhich of the following does the passage tell us about decision making?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'The brain is designed to enable quick decision making.\nQuick decision making can be improved.', NULL, NULL),
  ('aef53ea3-e143-5a33-81fb-35b36361c465'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'aef53ea3-e143-5a33-81fb-35b36361c465'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_READING_MULTIPLE - 2', E'Since 1980, the use of wind to produce electricity has been growing rapidly. In 1994 there were nearly 20,000 wind turbines worldwide, most grouped in clusters called wind farms that collectively produced 3,000 megawatts of electricity. Most were in Denmark (which got 3 percent of its electricity from wind turbines) and California (where 17,000 machines produced 1 percent of the state''s electricity, enough to meet the residential needs of a city as large as San Francisco). In principle, all the power needs of the United States could be provided by exploiting the wind potential of just three states—North Dakota, South Dakota, and Texas.\n\nBased on the information in the paragraph, which of the following best explains the term wind farms?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Types of power plant common in Denmark and California\nCollections of wind turbines producing electric power', NULL, NULL),
  ('f7132de7-3654-5bfe-bcb3-4a6c9bf163f1'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_READING_MULTIPLE', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'f7132de7-3654-5bfe-bcb3-4a6c9bf163f1'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_READING_MULTIPLE - 3', E'The differences in feeding preferences lead, in turn, to differences in migratory habits. The wildebeests follow, in their migration, the pattern of local rainfall. The other species do likewise. But when a new area is fueled by rain, the mammals migrate toward it in a set order to exploit it. The larger, less fastidious feeders, the zebras, move in first; the choosier, smaller wildebeests come later; and the smallest species of all, Thomson''s gazelle, arrives last. The later species all depend on the preparations of the earlier one, for the actions of the zebra alter the vegetation to suit the stomachs of the wildebeest, topi, and gazelle.\n\nAccording to the passage, which of the following is true of wildebeests?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'They tend to choose feeding areas in which the vegetation has been worn down.\nThey are relatively choosier than larger herbivores.', NULL, NULL),
  ('a2d401d1-93f0-5e5d-9d82-370d26bef258'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'a2d401d1-93f0-5e5d-9d82-370d26bef258'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS - 1', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'2, 3, 4, 1', NULL, NULL),
  ('779086a4-e716-5a9a-a3db-8981e4872cf7'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '779086a4-e716-5a9a-a3db-8981e4872cf7'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - RE_ORDER_PARAGRAPHS - 2', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, E'4, 1, 3, 2', NULL, NULL),
