  ('9d323cae-0d1e-5dab-83fa-5024909512ce'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '9d323cae-0d1e-5dab-83fa-5024909512ce'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP - 1', E'Today, many companies emphasize {{1}} in their operations. For example, packaging should be made from recyclable materials to ensure proper {{2}} . In households, using energy-efficient kitchen {{3}} helps reduce environmental impact.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.sustainability, 2.disposal, 3.appliances', NULL, NULL),
  ('b7af4cca-e1e1-5827-858a-44eddfde0279'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'b7af4cca-e1e1-5827-858a-44eddfde0279'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP - 2', E'The place had both mountains and a {{1}} . Every year, over 3.5 million {{2}} come to enjoy the scenery. There are also several miles of {{3}} that wind through the area.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.forest, 2.visitors, 3.trails', NULL, NULL),
  ('602496c0-cb9c-54b2-8d01-abc985835d8c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '602496c0-cb9c-54b2-8d01-abc985835d8c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DRAG_AND_DROP - 3', E'With the popularity of the gender equality campaign and the cultural change, the {{1}} roles of men as the {{2}} , and of women in which they stay at home, are {{3}} today.', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'1.traditional, 2.earner, 3.challenged', NULL, NULL),
  ('d2e9853c-db5a-53f4-863a-08d83c7bbaf5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'd2e9853c-db5a-53f4-863a-08d83c7bbaf5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_READING_SINGLE - 1', E'Many argue that art cannot be defined. We could go about this in several ways. Art is often considered as the process or product of deliberately arranging elements in a way that appeals to the senses or emotions. It encompasses a diverse range of human activities, creations and ways of expression, including music, literature, film, sculpture and paintings. The meaning of art is explored in a branch of philosophy known as aesthetics. At least, that is what Wikipedia claims.\n\nWhat is the main idea of the passage?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Art is a difficult and complex form to explain.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f9873837-6a2f-574d-a60b-803039e70918'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'f9873837-6a2f-574d-a60b-803039e70918'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_READING_SINGLE - 2', E'It is believed that Cushitic-speaking people were the first ethnic group to migrate to today’s Kenya. It is believed that they moved in from northern Africa somewhere around 2000 BCE. Then came the Arab Traders who started frequenting the Kenyan coast way back in the first century CE (Common Era). The Kenyan coast served host to communities of iron workers, subsistence farmers, hunters and fishermen who supported the economy with agriculture, fishing, metal production and trade with foreign countries.\n\nWhich of the following statements is not true with reference to Kenya?', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'Cushitic speaking people moved into today’s Kenyan territory around 2000 years ago.', NULL, NULL),
  ('90af4cdb-ffce-5fff-9664-566189bf1f06'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'MC_READING_SINGLE', E'READING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '90af4cdb-ffce-5fff-9664-566189bf1f06'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_READING_SINGLE - 3', E'Governments, business and many types of institutions collect, organise and record statistics. Statistics capture vital information about such things as the economy, population and the environment and therefore allow meaningful comparisons to be made. This can then inform decisions and plans made about such issues which in turn become public policies. While it may be the issues behind the statistics, rather than the statistics as such that command the public''s attention, it must be recognised that it is the figures that inform these issues.\n\nThe author considers statistics to be important because', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'they assist in driving public issues.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d3f5b5bd-c957-5354-91d0-e93ee78d9153'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'd3f5b5bd-c957-5354-91d0-e93ee78d9153'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT - 1', E'How people can recognize human faces? this is a hard but brilliant question. People should appreciate something. People can get visual information from faces and put a name on it. We can tell one’s identity, age, work, health condition, politics, and friends. Recognizing faces is amazing, difficult and a clever thing. In conclusion, people can get a lot out of faces.', 'c690b53d-6fee-5afd-bf00-3306b958508f'::uuid, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 70),
  ('c47c13fb-a162-54a3-b4db-59d488b225e6'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'c47c13fb-a162-54a3-b4db-59d488b225e6'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT - 2', E'About the importance of tea, one of the three most popular drinks in England in which the others are chocolate and coffee. Drinking tea in England was a symbol of social freedom, was very expensive and could only be ordered by men in public. Men had tea in coffee houses, making trades and chatting business, while women could only drink tea in private places or wait for their husbands to bring tea back home.', '58df5592-f873-56d4-9ac9-7243bc59f39f'::uuid, NULL, E'Tea is one of the three most popular drinks in England. Drinking tea in England was a symbol of social freedom. It was also very expensive and could only be ordered by men in public. To be more specific, men had tea in coffee houses, while women could only drink tea in private places.', NULL, 50, 70),
  ('69efa5cf-774f-5d93-9ee6-8ca50e48ab21'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT', E'SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '69efa5cf-774f-5d93-9ee6-8ca50e48ab21'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SUMMARIZE_SPOKEN_TEXT - 3', E'When this dog approaches some food, another dog''s playful snarls are played back. The dog seems curious, but the sound doesn''t stop it from taking the bone. Here a dog hears the growls of a dog being approached by a stranger, but these don''t deter it from grabbing the bone either. In another scenario the sound of a dog protecting its food is played back. This time the dog backs off. These experiments suggest the dogs can distinguish between different types of growls.', '83053b79-5bdf-5ab1-939d-e77523d3f302'::uuid, NULL, E'This lecture mainly talks about dogs growling. Firstly, the speaker emphasizes a dog''s curious snarls don''t stop another one from taking the bone. Also, she mentions the growls of a dog being approached by a stranger don''t deter it from grabbing the bone either. Lastly, the speaker believes these experiments suggest the dogs can distinguish between different types of growls. In conclusion, this lecture is very informative.', NULL, 50, 70),
  ('fc984e83-d5f1-5385-99f9-0667851be27c'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'fc984e83-d5f1-5385-99f9-0667851be27c'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE - 1', E'All domestic dogs belong to a single species that descended from wolves—despite vast differences in size, appearance, behavior and temperament among breeds.\nWhile dogs first became domesticated tens of thousands of years ago, the breeds we know today are largely the result of selection for certain traits by humans over the past several hundred years. “We have an enormous amount of diversity within the same species, and we can rarely observe such diversity in nature. So it’s a wonderful system to understand how evolution works within a short period of time.”\nEvolutionary biologist László Garamszegi of the Institute of Ecology and Botany in Hungary. He says that our playing with dogs is a key component of the human-canine bond.\n\nWhat are the characteristics of dogs in this passage?', '8629cab3-9eba-5e5a-8bed-20b363eebce5'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'All dogs evolved from wolves.\nPlay can help dogs bond with humans.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d9c01ee1-8516-5082-ad4a-d8ca36c53a1d'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'd9c01ee1-8516-5082-ad4a-d8ca36c53a1d'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE - 2', E'Woodblocks used for pictorial illustration became fairly common in 15th century Europe, but had been used long before that for printing designs on textiJes. Most of these were simple in design and quite crudely cut, but some were skillfully drawn and cut, while others even contained pictorial imagery.\nRecords show that woodblock printing on fabrics was practised by the Egyptians as early as 2000 years BC. The oldest existing printed fabric, which is Egyptian, dates from the 4th century. At the same time, the craft seems to have been widely established, even commonplace, elsewhere: for example, in India, Mexico and Peru, where the same techniques continue to be practised today. And the technique was almost certainly used by both the Japanese and the Chinese too.\n\nWhich of these countries still use woodblock printing on fabrics?', '6dd49593-d4d5-54a9-9b87-ebfefebebf36'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Peru\nIndia\nMexico', NULL, NULL),
  ('a669d32d-80ab-5f35-b362-78fa61813cfe'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'a669d32d-80ab-5f35-b362-78fa61813cfe'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_LISTENING_MULTIPLE - 3', E'All mammals have hair—commonly called fur when it''s on your cat or a koala. And the thickness of individual hairs varies from species to species. For example, elephant hairs are more than four times thicker than a strand from an adult human.\n"Normally, when the animal is larger, the hair tends to be thicker."\nUniversity of California, San Diego, materials scientist Wen Yang. She''s interested in how biological structures like hair hold up under stress. That interest comes from a desire to design better synthetic materials.\nYang''s team tested the tensile strength of hair from eight different mammal species, including humans. They subjected those hairs to increasing levels of tension until the fibers broke. The researchers assumed that thick hair—from giraffes, elephants and boars, for example, would be more robust. But they were wrong.\n\nWhich of the following statements about hair are correct?', 'fd1c9c99-9760-57a9-b8b1-984393915682'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Generally speaking, the size of an animal is directly proportional to the thickness of its hair.\nDifferent species have different hair thickness.', NULL, NULL),
  ('d3859ff2-c190-5af1-abc0-64805261a229'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'd3859ff2-c190-5af1-abc0-64805261a229'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN - 1', E'Urban gardens are becoming more {{0}} in large cities. Residents use {{1}} and empty lots to grow vegetables, herbs and flowers. These projects reduce food costs, improve air {{2}} and bring {{3}} together. Many schools now run small gardens so that {{4}} can learn where their food comes from.', 'ec5cb6b7-c4e2-5f5e-82ef-b763256745a9'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'["popular","rooftops","quality","neighbours","children"]', NULL, NULL),
  ('3d89e6c0-986e-531c-a35d-61bd41f6f905'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '3d89e6c0-986e-531c-a35d-61bd41f6f905'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN - 2', E'Sleep plays a {{0}} role in memory and learning. During deep sleep the brain {{1}} the information collected during the day and stores the {{2}} parts. Students who sleep less than six hours often struggle to {{3}} and perform worse in {{4}} than their well rested classmates.', '682905ed-092d-52ba-ad9f-f41236a21d90'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'["vital","sorts","important","concentrate","examinations"]', NULL, NULL),
  ('bc017fba-c3e9-52ae-b755-e104ea70b062'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN', E'FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'bc017fba-c3e9-52ae-b755-e104ea70b062'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_TYPE_IN - 3', E'The invention of the {{0}} press changed how {{1}} spread across Europe. Books that once took months to {{2}} by hand could be produced in days. As {{3}} fell, more people learned to read, and new ideas about science and {{4}} travelled quickly between cities.', 'ef8eedf9-c8b0-56b1-b4c8-348cb72e6bab'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'["printing","knowledge","copy","prices","religion"]', NULL, NULL),
  ('08b66a8c-2367-5712-9330-8cb4dbd10f48'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '08b66a8c-2367-5712-9330-8cb4dbd10f48'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY - 1', E'To enjoy a harmonious union with someone, we should ensure that we have plenty of sources of excitement, reassurance and stimulation outside of them. When we hit problems, we should be able to lean on other supports. The demand that another person compensates us for all that’s alarming, wearing or deficient in our lives is a mechanism for systematically destroying any relationship. Our conflicts and disappointments will at once feel more manageable when we stop asking our partner to function always as our long lost other half. The more we can survive without a relationship the greater will be that relationship’s chances of survival and fulfillment. We will truly give love a chance when we stop believing it can single-handedly save us.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', 'b99d6bd7-713a-5192-84a3-033e88eabecb'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The chance of survival and fulfillment of a relationship will be great, if we can survive without it. When we stop believing that love alone can save us, we will truly give love a chance.', NULL, NULL),
  ('b7e0f45c-bcb4-50a1-8d08-706cc2e695e5'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'b7e0f45c-bcb4-50a1-8d08-706cc2e695e5'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY - 2', E'A new investigation into shark populations in the waters off Australia has discoyered that there are two distinct species of Great White shark, one to the east and one to the west of Bass Strait. This was discovered by tagging large numbers of sharks in the coastal waters all round Australia. Rather to the investigators'' surprise, they found that while sharks from the east side certainly travelled to the west side of the continent and vice versa, they always returned to their home areas to breed. The two types of shark were found to have a distinct genetic make up, indicating that interbreeding has not taken place. The implication of these research findings is that sharks may be more susceptible to changes in local marine environments than had previously been thought.\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '3191a89c-7deb-5fc1-84bf-40cd240a1ae4'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'A recent research study has shown that Australian Great White shark populations have remained surprisingly distinct as, despite traveling long distances. these sharks do not breed away from their original areas. This means that local shark habitats may have a greater effect on sharks than has been believed up to now.', NULL, NULL),
  ('f34c8154-5c7a-5e9d-b75c-1e36555aeaef'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'f34c8154-5c7a-5e9d-b75c-1e36555aeaef'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - HIGHLIGHT_CORRECT_SUMMARY - 3', E'I actually want to caution against using the word ‘romance’. To me, romance can signify a lot of passion, chaos, instability — like we see in the movies. But this isn''t always healthy. Romance can be part of a relationship, but we should make sure that it''s not the definitive part. To me, the three great characteristics of a relationship are first, healthy communication. Are you able to express your needs, desires, and issues without a great deal of conflict? And is the other person open to hearing it? Number two is equality. Do you feel like an equal to your partner? Are you both putting in equal effort? And finally number three is trust. Do you feel your partner is loyal? Are you loyal to your partner? Do you ultimately have a safe relationship?\n\nClick on the paragraph that best relates to the recording.', '09ceb796-455f-509d-a3e6-14685388ea41'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Romance can be a part of a relationship, but it’s not everything. Healthy communication, equality and trust are all very important in a relationship.', NULL, NULL),
  ('8f37778e-074e-5f52-8b6c-931ad2a20019'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '8f37778e-074e-5f52-8b6c-931ad2a20019'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_LISTENING_SINGLE - 1', E'The atmosphere is a mixture of different gases and air assaults. We usually call it air. The atmosphere is very important to our lives, and we cannot live without it. Almost every living creature on earth breathes it. It surrounds earth and protects us from deadly rays and radiation from space.\n\nWhat is the talk mainly about?', '2bb4be20-f99a-529c-a38d-dc2e01f7ea4a'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'The functions of air', NULL, NULL),
  ('6c0f68f3-0dd1-546d-a20a-9321311b7ad2'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '6c0f68f3-0dd1-546d-a20a-9321311b7ad2'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_LISTENING_SINGLE - 2', E'There is a small town in belgium called waterloo. This small town became very famous because of napoleon''s last battle. A lot of his soldiers were killed and injured at waterloo. As a result, he was removed from his emperors throne and sent to St. Helena, where he died in eighteen twenty one.\n\nWhat is the main topic of the talk?', '97096be6-7ed0-5d77-ba9f-f11a030594ec'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Why Waterloo became well known', NULL, NULL),
  ('ce2b0550-ddbf-5018-b36a-183f19128585'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'MC_LISTENING_SINGLE', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'ce2b0550-ddbf-5018-b36a-183f19128585'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - MC_LISTENING_SINGLE - 3', E'A throbbing, pounding headache. Bright zigzagging lines across your field of vision. Sensitivity to light, lingering fatigue, disrupted sleep. A migraine can include any of these symptoms. While an incapacitating headache is one of the most common experiences of migraine, the word “headache” doesn’t really capture the wide array of experiences a migraine can entail. No two are alike, and some don’t even involve a headache.\n\nWhat does the speaker say about the symptoms of migraine?', 'a364837e-cded-511e-b768-d6a6f3483969'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'Migraine may include a variety of symptoms.', NULL, NULL),
  ('63818054-9c89-5462-a7ee-192ad40c0336'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', '63818054-9c89-5462-a7ee-192ad40c0336'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SELECT_MISSING_WORD - 1', E'Let''s see what''s happening on the seabed. Ok. So these really remarkable features are known as black smokers. Don''t forget, we''re now two and a half kilometers down. The light. It''s all pitch black. What we''re seeing is the lights from the submersible. So imagine you''re looking at this out from your porthole and it supports...\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '356e134d-1a9c-5b53-9b92-178a060d8b66'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'all this fabulous life', NULL, NULL),
  ('edc6a285-45e2-55e7-9c04-8cd63f108a7a'::uuid, TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-06 00:00:00+00', FALSE, E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'SELECT_MISSING_WORD', E'LISTENING', 'SHARED', NULL, 'APPROVED', 'edc6a285-45e2-55e7-9c04-8cd63f108a7a'::uuid, 1, NULL, TRUE, 0, NULL, E'DEMO22 - SELECT_MISSING_WORD - 2', E'The word science comes from a latin verb. Meaning to know science is a way of knowing. It emerges from our curiosity about ourselves and our world. Striving to understand is one of our basic drives who are scientists. Scientists are people who ask questions about nature and who believe that these questions can be answered. Scientists are explorers who are passionate about.\n\nAt the end of the recording the lost word or group of words has been replaced by a beep. Select the correct option to complete the recording.', '10610f71-0180-510e-927f-3d4cc93cfc24'::uuid, NULL, NULL, E'discovery', NULL, NULL),
